      "text": "To find the product of the base-seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) and then determine the sum of the digits of this product expressed in base seven, we'll first convert these base-seven numbers to base-ten, perform the multiplication, and convert the result back to base-seven. Finally, we'll sum the digits represented in base-seven.\n\n### Step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Convert the numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base-ten:**\n   \\[\n   24_7 = 2 \\times 7^1 + 4 \\times 7^0 = 2 \\times 7 + 4 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   30_7 = 3 \\times 7^1 + 0 \\times 7^0 = 3 \\times 7 + 0 = 21_{10}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the base-ten equivalents:**\n   \\[\n   18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert the product \\(378_{10}\\) back to base-seven.**\n   \n   To convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base-seven:\n   \n   - Determine how many full factors of 7 fit into 378.\n     \\[\n     378 \\div 7 = 54, \\text{ quotient: } 54\n     \\]\n   - Then, use the remaining remainder:\n     \\[\n     \\text{ remainder is } 378 - (54 \\times 7) = 378 - 378 = 0\n     \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Complete steps till 0: }\n     378 \\div 7 = 54, \\text{ quotient: } 54, \\text{ remainder: } 0\n     \\]\n   - Iterate to successive quotients:\n\n     - Quotient: \\(54, \\text{ remainder: } 378 - (54 \\times 7) = 378 - 378 = 0\\)\n     \\[\n     0 \\rightarrow 0\n     \\]\n\n4. **Sum up the digits in the base-seven conversion of 378:**\n   - Reading \\(378_{10}\\) as \\({\\bf \\underline{3}}\\text{ }{\\bf \\underline{7}}8_{\\textb{seven}},\\) the sum is:\n     \\[\n     3 + 7 + 8 = 18 \\text{ in base-ten}.\n     \\]\n   - Convert 18 back to base seven:\n     - \\(18 \\div 7 = 2\\) \n     - Remainder is: \\(18 - (2 \\times 7) = 18 - 14 = 4\\)\n     - In base-seven, they are \\( 204\\).\n\n```\nFinal Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{204}\n\\]",
