      "text": "We first convert the base seven numbers to base ten. $24_7$ converts to $\\frac{7+4=9\\times 7^1=7^2+7=8\\cdot 7}{}24_7$. $30_7$ converts to $\\frac{7+0}=7^1+0=7^1=8\\cdot 7$. Now we multiply the converted numbers in base ten to get 96. Now we convert our product to base seven by dividing by 7 and keeping track of remainders. ${\\frac{96}{7},\\frac{6}{7,}1=_{6}16}$.",
