      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we will first convert the given base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten. Then, we will perform the multiplication in base ten, converting the final result back to base seven. Finally, we will sum the digits of the resulting base seven number.\n\nLet's start by converting \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten:\n\n- The base seven number \\(24_7\\) represents \\(2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 14_{10}\\).\n- Similarly, the base seven number \\(30_7\\) represents \\(3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 21_{10}\\).\n\nNext, we multiply these base ten numbers:\n\n\\[14_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 294_{10}\\]\n\nNow we need to convert the product \\(294_{10}\\) back to base seven. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n294 \\div 7 &= 42 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\\\\n42 \\div 7 &= 6 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\\\\n6 \\div 7 &= 0 \\text{ remainder } 6 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base seven number \\(600_7\\).\n\nFinally, we will sum the digits of the base seven number \\(600_7\\):\n\n\\[6 + 0 + 0 = 6\\]\n\nSo, the base seven sum of the digits of the product of \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) is \\(6\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this step-by-step solution using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base ten number to base seven\r\ndef to_base_seven(n):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return \"0\"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % 7))\r\n        n //= 7\r\n    return ''.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Function to convert a base seven number (as a string) to base ten\r\ndef to_base_ten(s):\r\n    return sum(int(digit) * 7**exp for exp, digit in enumerate(reversed(s)))\r\n\r\n# Given base seven numbers 24_7 and 30_7\r\nnum1_base_seven = \"24\"\r\nnum2_base_seven = \"30\"\r\n\r\n# Convert to base ten\r\nnum1_base_ten = to_base_ten(num1_base_seven)\r\nnum2_base_ten = to_base_ten(num2_base_seven)\r\n\r\n# Perform multiplication in base ten\r\nproduct_base_ten = int(num1_base_ten) * int(num2_base_ten)\r\n\r\n# Convert the product back to base seven\r\nproduct_base_seven = to_base_seven(product_base_ten)\r\n\r\n# Sum the digits of the base seven product\r\nsum_of_digits = sum(int(digit) for digit in product_base_seven)\r\n\r\nprint(((product_base_seven, sum_of_digits)))\n```",
